h, web search, and Metis verification — behind a single MCP endpoint.\n\nIt speaks MCP over Streamable-HTTP (JSON-RPC 2.0 POST, SSE-`data:`-framed responses,`Mcp-Session-Id`) — the exact protocol Metis's MCP client and ARGUS already talk, so noexternal SDK is required.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQuick Start Ecosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Quick-Start-Ecosystem)\nciteturn12search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Quick Start Ecosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki ... Not in core fleet script (deploy separately — see runbook §9): Metis, LOGOS, SKOPOS, MOMUS/Treasury, GAIA/ATLAS, Signal Hunt, DIOSCURI, HELIOS, THEOROS, seventeen oracles, School.\n    ./scripts/deploy_ecosystem.sh            # 7 deploy steps + verify (17+ checks)\n    `\n\nService  | Local URL\n--- | ---\nFactory  | `http://localhost:9080` (API `:9081`)\nHub  | `http://localhost:9083`\nMesh  | `http://localhost:8090`\nARGUS  | `http://localhost:8787/health`\nMonitor  | `http://localhost:9100`\nPulse  | `http://localhost:5199`\nUNI lottery relayer  | `http://localhost:9195`\nEcosystem landing  | `https://modeldev.modelmarket.dev/` (after TLS)\n\nNot in core fleet script (deploy separately — see runbook §9): Metis, LOGOS, SKOPOS, MOMUS/Treasury, GAIA/ATLAS, Signal Hunt, DIOSCURI, HELIOS, THEOROS, seventeen oracles, School.\n\n## Production (public + TLS)\n    \n    `./scripts/quickstart_ecosystem.sh --public-url https://your-domain.example.com\n    sudo [email protected] ./scripts/setup-modelmarket-ssl.sh   # Hub TLS\n    # + certbot for the factory domain — see [Deployment](/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Deployment)\n    ./scripts/verify_ecosystem_full.sh\n\n## Oracle host (separate machine by default)\n\n`deploy_ecosystem.sh` does not deploy the seventeen oracles. On the oracle host:\n    \n    `sudo [email protected] ./scripts/setup-oracles-platon-on-host.sh\n    ./scripts/announce-platon-oracles.sh     # then federate from the factory host\n    `\n\n## On-chain (optional, Base mainnet 8453)\n    \n    `./scripts/deploy_ecosystem_base.sh broadcast   # FakeUSDT / Escrow / NFT\n    ./scripts/deploy_lottery_base.sh broadcast      # AIAgentLottery\n    `\n\n## Monitor mode: LIVE vs UNI\n\nThe Alien Monitor runs in universe (self-contained simulation) by default. To bind it to the real chain (Base) at deploy time:\n    \n    `ALIEN_MODE=real ./scripts/deploy_alien_monitor.sh    # or: --live\n    `\n\nLIVE reads the live contract addresses from `chain_net` and skips the embedded dev chains.\n\nFull details, troubleshooting, ports, and the RU/ES translations: `docs/quickstart-ecosystem-deploy.md`.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nmixture-of-agents · GitHub Topics · GitHub (https://vpn.luca-server.com/px/aHR0cHM6Ly9naXRodWIuY29tL3RvcGljcy9taXh0dXJlLW9mLWFnZW50cz9vPWRlc2Mmcz11cGRhdGVk)\nciteturn12search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; ### alexar76 / metis\n### alexar76 / metis\n\nStar\n\n  * Code\n  * Issues\n  * Pull requests\n  * Discussions\n\nMetis (μῆτις) — distributed cognitive layer over any LLM. Understanding Council → confidence gate (fail-closed) → layered MoA → verifier-with-retry, with DGPD depth gating, memory, economy metering, and an OpenAI-compatible API. A loosely-coupled ecosystem peer: runs fully standalone; every ecosystem hook is optional.\n\npython mcp verification multi-agent reasoning llm mixture-of-agents openai-compatible aimarket aicom\n\n  * Updated Sep 5, 2026\n  * Python\n\n### pealmeida / gateswarm\n\nStar\n\n  * Code\n  * Issues\n  * Pull requests\n\nCut LLM costs 90%+. Route every prompt to the cheapest capable model. 6-level complexity score in 12 ms. Zero GPU.\n\npython moa cost-optimization ai-gateway mixture-of-agents llm-routing model-routing prompt-classification\n\n  * Updated Sep 4, 2026\n  * TypeScript\n\n### tylerreckart / arbiter\n\nSponsor\n\nStar\n\n  * Cod